<article class="env-lemma" id="5F8C">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/5F8C">Lemma <span data-tag="5F8C">2.4.4.1</span>.</a> Let $p: \calC \rightarrow \calD $ be an inner fibration of $\infty $-categories, and let $X,Y \in \calC $. The induced map $\phi : \Hom ^{\rght }_{\calC }(X,Y) \rightarrow \Hom ^{\rght }_{\calD }(p(X),p(Y))$ is a Kan fibration. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Since $p$ is an inner fibration, the induced map $\widetilde{\phi }: \calC _{/X} \rightarrow \calD _{/p(X)} \times _{\calD } \calC $ is a right fibration by Proposition <a href="/tag/F390" data-tag="F390">2.1.2.1</a>. We note that $\phi $ is obtained from $\widetilde{\phi }$ by restricting to the fiber over the vertex $Y$ of $\calC $. Thus $\phi $ is a right fibration; since the target of $\phi $ is a Kan complex, $\phi $ is a Kan fibration by Lemma <a href="/tag/4508" data-tag="4508">2.1.3.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>